            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 22-year-old woman presents with headache and an acquired cranial nerve VI palsy. The differential diagnosis and work-up were negative. The causes of cranial nerve VI palsy in young patients are discussed. Follow-up for patients in this age group is also discussed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
